WEBVTT - Customer Incident Escalation Interview

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.500
<v Interviewer> Can you describe how high-priority customer incidents are handled from the moment they are reported?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
<v Support Lead> Absolutely. The process starts when the Customer Support Agent logs the incident ticket in Jira Service Management.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Support Lead> Next, the Incident Manager reviews the ticket and determines if the incident is critical (Sev-1) or standard severity.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Support Lead> If it is critical, the Incident Manager immediately alerts the On-Call Engineering team and opens a bridge war room.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Support Lead> If it is not critical, the ticket is routed to the Tier 2 Support Queue for standard troubleshooting.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:34.000
<v Support Lead> For critical issues, On-Call Engineering develops and tests an emergency hotfix in staging.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Support Lead> Once tested, DevOps deploys the fix to production and verifies system health metrics.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.000
<v Support Lead> Finally, the Customer Support Agent updates the customer with the incident resolution and closes the ticket.
